The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!vsp1->info->uapi)
	vsp1_drm_cleanup(vsp1);
Reason:
This unconditional call to `vsp1_drm_cleanup()` for all devices without uapi (including Gen4 VSPX) causes a NULL pointer dereference because Gen4 VSPX devices require `vsp1_vspx_cleanup()` instead. The cleanup function `vsp1_destroy_entities()` does not distinguish between DRM and VSPX variants, leading to an invalid access when the module is unloaded.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!vsp1->info->uapi) {
	if (vsp1->info->version == VI6_IP_VERSION_MODEL_VSPX_GEN4)
		vsp1_vspx_cleanup(vsp1);
	else
		vsp1_drm_cleanup(vsp1);
}
Reason:
The fix checks the IP version before calling the appropriate cleanup function. For Gen4 VSPX devices, it calls `vsp1_vspx_cleanup()`, while for other devices without uapi, it continues to call `vsp1_drm_cleanup()`. This matches the initialization logic and prevents the NULL pointer dereference.

